WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.560
Michael Bloomberg is reportedly preparing
to enter the presidential race.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.540
Michael Bloomberg is a 77 year old billionaire
originally from right down the road from our

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.420
studio in Brighton, Massachusetts.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.250
He's been the mayor of New York city.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.370
He has switched from Republican to Democrat
in the last year or two.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.310
He's been an independent at different points
in his life.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:44.180
I believe he's always been independent minded
to the extent that that means anything in

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:50.150
the modern political status quo of a relatively
narrow Overton window of what's acceptable

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.310
and his idea of running for president is absolutely
terrible.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:57.710
Now I know that there's a lot of people just
tweeting stuff like we don't need another

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.140
billionaire in the race.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.280
Some a sentiment I shared on Twitter and that's
true.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:08.220
I mean this would make a Michael Bloomberg
the second a billionaire in the democratic

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.080
primary along with Tom Stier.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.680
And if you won the primary, the race becomes
73 year old billionaire against 77 year old

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.820
billionaire.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.790
Not exactly the wide range of choice that
you would imagine you could get from a country

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.440
of 340 million people.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.440
Okay.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.440
That, that's fine.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.620
Um, but I actually don't think, listen, if
I had to have a billionaire as president who

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:38.060
has political experience and is a smart politician,
if you frame it up that way, of course I want

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.580
Bloomberg over Donald Trump.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.510
Of course I want Bloomberg over many other
billionaires.

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:49.780
Michael Bloomberg to me is a combination of
a guy who has, uh, made himself very rich

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:56.900
